Run fwts tests in the power states category (as returned by fwts --power-states).
These run automatically by default and require no user intervention.

This includes the following tests (based on x86_64, may vary on other arches):

s3              S3 suspend/resume test.
s3power         S3 power loss during suspend test (takes minimum of 10 minutes to run).
s4              S4 hibernate/resume test.

Note: s3/s3power may cause crashes if system does not suspend/resume properly.
s3power will abort on systems with no batter installed. s4 tests hibernate
(suspend to disk) and may cause crashes, additionally some UEFI based Beaker
systems may not reboot correctly upon resume from hibernation and will require
manually setting the boot order or reprovisioning the machine to recover.

